values ('fq_shard_063', 'Ancient Stone Must Step Aside', 'story', 'S', 'CHILDREN_OF_THE_SHARD', 'SEVERANCE_FAULTLINE', 'Gigantic Jotunns are drawn to the Severance Faultline''s deep mineral activity — the same geological turbulence that the Shard''s healing effort is generating as it tries to reconnect the fractured substrate. The Jotunns are geological entities; they do not interfere with the Shard''s work intentionally, but their presence creates seismic interference that disrupts the aethel reconnection at the molecular level. Elder Malakor speaks with genuine sorrow about this: ''They are ancient as the world, and they must still move aside, because the world''s healing cannot wait for their convenience.'' Bind them to the deep stone. Quest giver: High Priestess Lyr at Sanctum Inner Chamber.', '{"npc_id": "npc_high_priest", "name": "Oracle Seraphel", "location": "SEVERANCE_FAULTLINE"}'::jsonb, '{"min_level": 63, "reputation_required": 1545, "required_quests": ["fq_shard_062"]}'::jsonb, '[{"type": "kill", "target": "GIGANTIC_JOTUNN", "count": 3, "description": "Bind to earth. [Gigantic Jotunn]"}, {"type": "collect", "target": "core_fragment", "count": 1, "description": "Collect core fragment (x1). [Item: Core Fragment]"}]'::jsonb, '{"exp": 3750, "currency": 1875, "crd": 906, "rep": 1145, "items": [{"item_id": "aethel_core_shard", "quantity": 1}], "reputation": 50}'::jsonb, false, false, 'fq_shard_064', false, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'quest_shard.json', 62)
